  "reasoning_text": "We need ISCO radii for Kerr a* = 0.5.\n\nFormula: r_ISCO in equatorial plane (Boyer-Lindquist):\nr = M { 3 + Z2 ∓ sqrt(3 - a*² + Z1) } where plus for prograde (smaller r) with sign convention... Actually:\n\nZ1 = 1 + (1 - a²)^{1/3} [ (1 + a)^{1/3} + (1 - a)^{1/3} ]\nZ2 = sqrt(3 a² + Z1²)\n\nr_± = 3 + Z2 ∓ sqrt(3 - a² + Z1)  (in units of M), where r_- corresponds to prograde (direct) orbit.\n\nHere a = a* = dimensionless spin parameter (a/M). a = 0.5, a² = 0.25.\n\nCompute:\n1 - a² = 0.75\n(0.75)^{1/3}: cube root of 0.75. 0.75^(1/3): ln0.75 = -0.28768, /3 = -0.09589, exp = 0.90856. So ≈ 0.908560.\n\n(1 + a)^{1/3} = 1.5^{1/3}: ln1.5=0.405465, /3=0.135155, exp=1.144714. ≈ 1.14471.\n\n(1 - a)^{1/3} = 0.5^{1/3} = 0.793701.\n\nSum: 1.144714 + 0.793701 = 1.938415. Multiply by 0.908560: 1.938415 × 0.908560 ≈ ?\n\n1.938415 × 0.9 = 1.744574; ×0.00856 = 0.016593; total ≈ 1.761167. Let's compute precisely: 0.908560 × 1.938415.\n\n1.938415 × 0.908560 = 1.938415 × (0.9 + 0.008560) = 1.7445735 + 0.016593... 1.938415×0.00856 = 0.016592... compute: 1.938415×0.008 = 0.0155073; ×0.00056 = 0.0010855; sum 0.0165928. Total 1.761166I could not confirm this. In my answer I will claim only what I actually verified, and say plainly which check failed.",
